{"abstract":[{"text":"Learn how to add AstronomyKit to your project and perform basic astronomical calculations.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Getting Started with AstronomyKit","modules":[{"name":"AstronomyKit"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/TimeAndObservers"],"anchor":"Essentials"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/GettingStarted"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"AstronomyKit provides a type-safe Swift interface for astronomical calculations. This article walks you through installation and your first calculations."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Installation","anchor":"Installation","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add AstronomyKit to your Swift package:"}]},{"code":["dependencies: [","    .package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/AstronomyKit\", from: \"4.0.0\")","]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Or in Xcode: "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"File → Add Package Dependencies","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and enter the repository URL."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Your First Calculations","anchor":"Your-First-Calculations","level":2},{"type":"heading","text":"Import the Package","anchor":"Import-the-Package","level":3},{"code":["import AstronomyKit"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"Set Up Your Observer Location","anchor":"Set-Up-Your-Observer-Location","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Most astronomical calculations require an observer location on Earth:"}]},{"code":["\/\/ New York City",